# Zap Platform rules

Read [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) and [`Zap_Platform_Codex_Prompt.md`](../../Zap_Platform_Codex_Prompt.md) before planning or changing code. The latter is the authoritative contract.

- Preserve the Node.js/TypeScript Fastify modular monolith, React/Vite apps, Hostinger-compatible SQL migrations and existing module boundaries.
- Respect RBAC and tenant isolation for `platform_admin`, `company_admin`, `attendant` and `professional`.
- Keep SQL behind the API; avoid new frameworks, dependencies, services, caches and oversized files.
- Keep all user-facing content in natural Brazilian Portuguese (`pt-BR`).
- Make scoped changes, run relevant checks/tests, and report changed files and pending issues.
- Never perform destructive database operations without explicit approval.
